# =============================================================================
# AkbasCore 3.2 — SEASC + Composite Compass Foundry
# Standardized Evidential Activation-Steering Core
#
# REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION / SINGLE-CELL COLAB DEMO
#
# WHAT CHANGED FROM 3.1?
# ----------------------
# The SEASC motor, CUDA kernel, physical dose and DRA envelope are unchanged.
# Only the Compass Foundry is updated.
#
# 3.1:
#   Runtime direction = Subspace-Fisher compass F_L
#
# 3.2:
#   Matched sample directions are combined into BANK_MEAN B_L.
#   Fisher is retained as the geometric reference:
#
#       c_L = <F_L, B_L>
#       R_L = normalize(B_L - c_L F_L)
#
#   Composite compass:
#
#       A_L(beta) = normalize(
#           c_L F_L + beta * sqrt(1-c_L^2) R_L
#       )
#
#   beta = 0.0  -> Fisher component / 3.1-compatible reference direction
#   beta = 1.0  -> BANK_MEAN exactly (AkbasCore 3.2 reference lock)
#
# TEST 162 showed that BANK_MEAN exceeded Fisher at the stronger tested
# steering regimes while Fisher remains useful as a geometric reference.
# Therefore Fisher is NOT discarded: it remains inside Compass Foundry
# for decomposition and telemetry, while beta=1 uses BANK_MEAN at runtime.
#
# Runtime remains static:
#   NO cosine gate / cap / brake / controller / radar / JVP.
#
# Reference Core:
#   Composite Compass Foundry
#   + Frozen-Norm Direct Dose
#   + Static Normalized DRA Envelope
#
# Reference: Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct · BF16 · A100
# AkbasCore / SEASC / Compass Foundry — Akbaş, 2026
# =============================================================================

